## Graphical Abstract
## Antibacterial photodynamic inactivation by light-driven self-disinfecting textile
## Highlights：
• Light-driven antibacterial textile material was achieved by introducing PCN-224.
• PCN-224 nanoparticles were in situ grown on woven cotton fabrics.
• PCN-224/WCF showed high efficient photobactericidal activity.
• MTT assay showed low cytotoxicity and good biocompatibility
• The DPBF studies revealed ROS was generated via Type II mechanism.
